# HyperBabel React Demo — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the Firebase block.
# .env.local is gitignored so your local values never leak.

# ── HyperBabel API endpoint ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Points at production by default — the right value for almost every
# integrator. Override only if you operate HyperBabel on a private domain.
VITE_HB_API_URL=https://api.hyperbabel.com/api/v1

# ── Firebase (required for sign-in AND optional web push) ─────────────────
# The demo uses Customer Auth pattern B1 (Firebase Direct Exchange):
#
#   1. User signs in with Firebase Auth in the browser
#      → Firebase ID token
#   2. POST /customer/auth/firebase-exchange with that token
#      → short-lived HyperBabel customer JWT (1h access, 30d refresh)
#   3. The customer JWT is attached to every API call.
#      The HyperBabel org API key NEVER ships in the browser bundle —
#      api.js throws at startup if it sees one.
#
# Setup checklist:
#   • Create a Firebase project: https://console.firebase.google.com
#   • Authentication → Sign-in method → enable Email/Password (and Anonymous
#     if you want the kiosk-mode button)
#   • Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains → add this app's origin
#     (localhost is allow-listed by default)
#   • Project Settings → Your apps → Web → register, then copy values below
#   • Allow-list this Firebase project in HyperBabel Console →
#     Customer Auth → Add Firebase project
#
# Web SDK config values are CLIENT-SAFE (Firebase publishes this exact
# shape for browser apps) — they are kept out of git here only because
# they're org-specific, not because they are secret.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── Web Push (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Add this VAPID key only if you want browser push notifications. The demo
# silently disables push when it's blank — all other features still work.
# Get it from Firebase Console → Cloud Messaging → Web Push Certificates.
VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=

# ── Real-Time & RTC ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No additional keys needed — credentials are minted by HyperBabel and
# fetched with the customer JWT above:
#   POST /rtm/token        → signed real-time channel token
#   POST /rtm/rtc/token    → RTC token + app config (video calls, live streams)
